@page "/components/bottom-nav-bar"

<PageTitle>Bottom Nav Bar — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Bottom Nav Bar</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A pill of icon tabs for the bottom of a phone screen, after Arunachalam's bottom navigation
    bar on 21st.dev. Only the active tab shows its name; picking another slides its name out on a
    spring while the previous one folds away.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="BottomNavBarExample.razor"><BottomNavBarExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">As page navigation</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Give the tabs an <code>Href</code> and they are links; <code>Active</code> marks the current
    page with <code>aria-current="page"</code>. A folded name is still in the markup, so every
    tab keeps its accessible name even while it shows only its icon.
</p>
<Example Source="BottomNavBarLinks.razor"><BottomNavBarLinks /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Sticky bottom</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>StickyBottom</code> pins the bar above the bottom edge of the window, centred. It covers
    the last 72px or so of the page, so give the page that much padding at the bottom.
</p>
<Example Source="BottomNavBarSticky.razor"><BottomNavBarSticky /></Example>
